      "level": 2,
      "content": "GANDHIAN MASS STRUGGLE – COMPLETE & EXHAUSTIVE EXPLANATION"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The 1919–1934 period forms the core phase of Gandhian mass struggles in the Indian freedom movement.",
        "The Rowlatt Act and Jallianwala Bagh Massacre of 1919 transformed political resistance into a nationwide mass movement.",
        "The Non-Cooperation Movement (1920–1922) united Hindu and Muslim communities alongside the Khilafat Movement.",
        "The Swarajist Phase (1923–1927) focused on entering legislative councils to oppose colonial administration from within.",
        "The Civil Disobedience Movement (1930–1934) escalated resistance by directly defying colonial laws, leading to constitutional talks like the Round Table Conferences and Poona Pact."
      ],
      "id": "yvyw4hs"
    },
